// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/validation_bounds.t27 -- the shared validators, and the one that manufactures
; a number
; This contract owns src/trios/validation.rs: the QR token grammar, the Telegram id grammar and
; its numeric bound, the contract of the two clamps, and the boundary the clamps may not cross.
; It owns no price, no rate and no absence rendering -- turbobaby/pricing-honesty owns "absent
; is not zero" and this file hands absence to it rather than describing it. It owns no identity:
; an id that passes a bound is a well-formed integer and nothing more, and
; turbobaby/request-identity owns who a request is. It owns no admin write bound:
; turbobaby/catalog-write owns what an admin form may produce, and the write-path parser named
; below is cited here only as the honest counterexample to the clamp. ASCII only (L3), English identifiers only (LANG-EN).
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). src/trios/validation.rs is 502 lines and exports 13 public items.
; FIVE of them are reached by live code and EIGHT by nothing at all -- not by src/, not by
; tests/. The five that are reached split three ways along the line D9 draws, and nobody has
; drawn it: parse_int_in_range and parse_finite_float_in_range REFUSE a bad input with the field
; named; normalize_media_url REWRITES one and cannot refuse at all (src/trios/validation.rs:249
; returns String and never Result, and :264 prefixes a scheme-less input -- cited as :239 until
; 2026-09-22, which was one line off from the day ed0ba9c wrote it; see the note under the census)
; -- it is counted apart from the parsers because calling it a refusal would be false; and
; clamp_finite_in_range and clamp_finite_non_negative REPLACE a bad input with a NUMBER and say
; nothing. Only the last two manufacture a quantity, and only they are this file's subject.
; (Re-measured 2026-09-22: was 502 lines, 13 items and five reached; now 542, 15 and SEVEN, still
; eight by nothing. 2c21df1 added INIT_DATA_MAX_BYTES and init_data_size_admits, the client's
; mirror of the server's initData cap, and src/ui/api/client.rs imports both. Neither refuses,
; rewrites or substitutes a bad input, so the three-way split and its subject are unchanged; the
; census constants below carry the correction.)
; clamp_finite_in_range has exactly four live call sites, all four in src/api/quest.rs
; (:95, :96, :276, :282), all four on a coordinate, and all four pass a fallback of 0.0 that sits
; INSIDE the range they just checked. So a NaN latitude, an out-of-range latitude and a genuine
; reading of zero leave that function as the same f64, and the consumer of the JSON at
; src/api/quest.rs:102-110 -- a customer's quest map -- cannot tell which it got. The doc comment
; at src/trios/validation.rs:162-165 names that exact outcome as the bug the WRITE path was fixed
; to stop: a typo routed to "(0, 0) - Gulf of Guinea". The read path still ships it, for a
; different reason, through a helper whose name says it is safe. And the input is already zeroed
; once before the clamp is asked: src/api/quest.rs:95 reads the column with
; .unwrap_or(0.0), so a renamed or missing column reaches the clamp as a finite, in-range,
; perfectly publishable zero and the clamp passes it through untouched.
; --
; DECISIONS.md D9 (:116-133) is the rule, and it is quoted rather than paraphrased because the
; family it names is exactly this file's subject: "Three separate constructs in this tree turn an
; unknown number into a confident zero" (DECISIONS.md:118), and money fields are therefore
; nullable, "routed through none of the three constructs above. Absent renders as a dash --
; never 0, never an average, never a 'from' price" (DECISIONS.md:126-130). The two clamps here
; are a FOURTH and FIFTH member of that family, not counted by D9 because D9 was written about
; the strain money path. They are worse than the three D9 lists in one measurable respect:
; try_get_warn! at src/db/macros.rs:28-44 at least emits a tracing::warn on the substitution, and
; a grep of src/trios/validation.rs:203-231 for tracing returns ZERO. The clamps are the silent
; members of the family.
; --
; WHERE THE BRIEF IS REFUTED. Three corrections, each measured, each a result rather than an
; aside.
; (1) D9's own citation for the first construct is stale. DECISIONS.md:122 cites the clamp
; closure at "src/db/strains.rs:123-129, 165-171". Measured 2026-09-21 the two closures open at
; src/db/strains.rs:129 and :171 and close at :135 and :177 -- both spans are off by six lines.
; The other three D9 citations hold exactly: migrations/008_strains_full_seed.sql:21 is the
; NOT NULL DEFAULT 0 on price_per_gram, src/db/macros.rs:28-44 is try_get_warn!, and
; migrations/059_cart_tables.sql:19 is the unit_price CHECK.
; (2) The brief asks for QrToken and TelegramId "and anything else it exports" from
; src/trios/validation.rs. That file exports NEITHER. Both are type aliases declared in
; src/trios/core.rs -- pub type TelegramId = i64; at :444 and pub type QrToken = String; at :447
; -- re-exported by src/trios/mod.rs:27 and merely imported by the validator at
; src/trios/validation.rs:3. They are aliases and not newtypes, so validate_qr_token returns a
; plain String and the type system does nothing whatever to keep an unvalidated string out of a
; QrToken slot. The validation is the only barrier, which makes the next correction matter.
; (3) The brief asks which other modules import the clamp. Measured: none. clamp_finite_in_range
; has one importer (src/api/quest.rs:2) and four call sites; clamp_finite_non_negative has one
; caller anywhere (src/db/orders.rs:1186) and it guards an admin revenue figure. The eight
; unreached exports include validate_qr_token itself: the live QR scan path builds its own
; grammar at src/api/quest.rs:617-626, which requires only 1..=200 characters, checks no alphabet
; at all, and accepts the token under either of two body keys. The strict 16-character
; alphanumeric grammar is shipped, tested, and enforced on nothing. Both grammars are pinned
; below and their disagreement is a named function, because a reader who greps for
; validate_qr_token will otherwise believe the live path is the one it describes.
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It ships no QR token: nothing in it is 16 alphanumeric characters,
; in a constant, a test or a comment, because a spec is a public file and a plausible token is a
; guess at a real one. The grammar is pinned by a character count and a class predicate instead.
; It ships no Telegram id, real or invented: the only large integers here are 2^53-1 and its
; successor, which are properties of IEEE 754 double precision and of nothing's account. It holds
; no f64 and cannot: no contract in this corpus declares one -- re-run over all 43 .t27 files on
; 2026-09-21 at review and still 0, pinned below as F64_DECLARATIONS_IN_CORPUS so the next reader
; re-runs a number instead of trusting this sentence -- so finiteness travels here as a boolean
; argument and magnitude as a scaled integer, which is honest about what the language can check
; and refuses to imply that a float was evaluated. It computes no price and renders no
; absence -- there is no function here from an unknown to a number, and that missing function IS
; the specification. It carries nothing from D14: no renter, handle, phone, plate, key code, debt,
; purchase cost or personal note, in a constant, a fixture or a comment. The two coordinates that
; do appear are a capital city's, lifted from the shipped regression test they exist to explain.
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-validation-bounds;

pub const KIND : str = "validator-contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/validation-bounds";
pub const NAME : str = "Shared validators and the clamp boundary";

; --- Ownership edges ------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The pinned compiler lowers a brace import to an empty UseDecl, which the gate rejects, so a
; cross-contract edge is a string naming the owner's ID plus a test asserting the literal. None
; of these four vocabularies is restated here; each arrives as an abstract argument.
pub const REUSES_PRICING_ID : str = "turbobaby/pricing-honesty";
pub const REUSES_RIDE_RUNTIME_ID : str = "turbobaby/ride-runtime";
pub const REUSES_REQUEST_IDENTITY_ID : str = "turbobaby/request-identity";
pub const REUSES_CATALOG_WRITE_ID : str = "turbobaby/catalog-write";
pub const REUSE_EDGE_COUNT : u8 = 4;

; What each edge supplies, as the abstract thing this file's functions actually take.
pub const ABSENCE_INPUT : str = "absence is not zero, and the rendering of it, owned by the pricing contract";
pub const LEGITIMATE_CLAMP_INPUT : str = "the bounded control clamp owned by the ride runtime contract";
pub const IDENTITY_INPUT : str = "proof outcome supplied by the request identity contract";
pub const WRITE_BOUND_INPUT : str = "admin write ceilings owned by the catalog write contract";

; The clamp this file borrows as its legitimate SHAPE, named by the declaration its owner gives
; it and never by a line number. Its bounds, its units and its rate belong to that contract; what
; this file needs from it is only its shape, recorded as two booleans below.
; --
; RE-MEASURED 2026-09-21 at review, and the sentence above used to read "the one clamp in this
; corpus that is legitimate", which is a uniqueness claim over specs/ and was written when the
; corpus was smaller. Counted today by grepping specs/ for a pub fn whose name contains clamp:
; SIX files declare one. Four of them are this file's own models of the construct it judges
; (clamp_outcome, clamp_result, clamp_is_legitimate, clamp_call_is_permitted); the other five
; files are turbobaby/happy-hour with clamp_discount_percent, turbobaby/loyalty-ledger with
; clamp_would_fire and clamp_fires_under_the_guard, turbobaby/order-money with
; order_money_clamp_at_zero, turbobaby/ride-runtime with clamp_horizontal_control, and
; turbobaby/upload-media with sanitizer_clamp_can_fire.
; This file does NOT adjudicate any of those five. USE_BOUNDED_CONTROL is a verdict about what a
; value steers and who reads it, which is each owner's subject and not this one's, so no
; legitimacy verdict is passed on a sibling's declaration here and none is implied. What is
; claimed, and all that is claimed, is that clamp_horizontal_control is the declaration this file
; takes its legitimate shape FROM -- an interval that defines the quantity, an output that steers
; something and is never published. The count is pinned as a constant so the sentence cannot
; quietly turn back into a uniqueness claim the next time the corpus grows.
pub const CORPUS_FILES_DECLARING_A_CLAMP_FN : u8 = 6;
pub const SIBLING_FILES_DECLARING_A_CLAMP_FN : u8 = 5;
pub const CLAMP_FNS_DECLARED_HERE : u8 = 4;
pub const SIBLING_CLAMP_OWNER_IDS : [5]str = [
    "turbobaby/happy-hour",
    "turbobaby/loyalty-ledger",
    "turbobaby/order-money",
    "turbobaby/ride-runtime",
    "turbobaby/upload-media"
];
pub const LEGITIMATE_CLAMP_IS_A_UNIQUENESS_CLAIM : bool = false;
pub const SIBLING_CLAMP_LEGITIMACY_IS_JUDGED_HERE : bool = false;
pub const LEGITIMATE_CLAMP_DECLARATION : str = "clamp_horizontal_control";
pub const LEGITIMATE_CLAMP_SATURATES_AT_THE_BOUND : bool = true;
pub const LEGITIMATE_CLAMP_OUTPUT_IS_EVER_PUBLISHED : bool = false;

